1	select	Select an option
1	option	Can you tell me more about your sons?
2	line	Player	Can you tell me more about your sons?
2	line	Timfraku	My first son is Tamayu. After him was born Tinsay. And after him was born Tiadeche.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Can you tell me more about Tamayu?
3	line	Player	Can you tell me more about Tamayu?
3	line	Timfraku	Tamayu was a natural born hunter. He killed his first monkey at the age of three!
3	action	Shows initial brother queries
2	option	Can you tell me more about Tinsay?
3	line	Player	Can you tell me more about Tinsay?
3	line	Timfraku	Tinsay was brought up to be a priest. Be careful with him - he has acted strange since the accident.
3	line	Player	What accident?
3	line	Timfraku	It involved Jogres. We don't talk about it.
3	action	Shows initial brother queries
2	option	Can you tell me more about Tiadeche?
3	line	Player	Can you tell me more about Tiadeche?
3	line	Timfraku	Tiadeche always wanted to hunt fish. However, he has not had much success.
3	line	Player	How come?
3	line	Timfraku	He needs to improve his technique - but he does not heed my advice.
3	action	Shows initial brother queries
2	option	Return to previous menu
3	action	initial
1	option	Where can I find your sons?
2	line	Player	Where can I find your sons?
2	line	Timfraku	On our island of Karamja. They will not have fled far.
2	action	initial
1	option	Is there anything I need?
2	line	Player	Is there anything I need?
2	line	Timfraku	Patience, Bwana, patience.
2	line	Timfraku	And good conversation skills.
2	action	initial
1	option	I'll be back later.
2	line	Player	I'll be back later.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about Village.
2	action	Shows previous village questions.
0	section	Attempting to enter any of the brother's huts in Tai Bwo Wannai Village
1	box	You do not have permission to enter here
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Tiadeche
1	line	Player	Are you Tiadeche?
1	line	Tiadeche	I am.
1	line	Player	Tiadeche, I bring good news. Trufitus has communed with the gods - your village is once again safe.
1	line	Player	Your father requests that you return to the village.
1	line	Tiadeche	I will return only when I have caught a Karambwan.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What is a Karambwan?
2	line	Player	What is a Karambwan?
2	line	Tiadeche	You don't know? The Karambwan is a species of octopus native to these waters.
2	line	Tiadeche	They have a monopoly on its sale in the pirate town of Brimhaven.
2	action	initial
1	option	When will you be finished?
2	line	Player	When will you be finished?
2	line	Tiadeche	At this rate, it could take forever.
2	line	Player	We don't have forever.
2	line	Tiadeche	Sometimes, oblivion is all I crave...
2	action	initial
1	option	Is there anything I can do to help?
2	line	Player	Is there anything I can do to help?
2	line	Tiadeche	I just don't know. You can try.
2	line	Player	What would you have me do?
2	line	Tiadeche	Something ... helpful?
2	action	end
1	option	How are you fishing for the Karambwan?
2	line	Player	How are you fishing for the Karambwan?
2	line	Tiadeche	I'm trying to catch them with a net as they swim by.
2	line	Player	And ... ?
2	line	Tiadeche	They keep fighting loose of the twining.
2	action	initial
0	section	Talking to Tiadeche again
1	cond	If the player uses a raw, cooked, or poisoned Karambwan on Tiadeche:
2	line	Tiadeche	I refuse to take your offerings. I must catch this Karambwan myself.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player gives Tiadeche an empty Karambwan vessel:
2	line	Player	Tiadeche, instead of using your net, try using this vessel.
2	box	You hand over the Karambwan vessel to Tiadeche.
2	line	Tiadeche	What is it?
2	line	Player	It has been specially constructed to catch Karambwan. Once they enter it, they cannot return..
2	line	Tiadeche	As you say, Bwana.
2	box	Tiadeche attempts to use the Karambwan vessel.
2	line	Tiadeche	This vessel is useless! The Karambwan are not even interested in entering it!
2	action	
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player gives Tiadeche a raw Karambwanji:
2	line	Player	I've been told that the Karambwan feed only on the Karambwanji. This will make good bait.
2	box	You hand over a raw Karambwanji to Tiadeche.
2	line	Tiadeche	The Holy Friend? Bwana, it is sacrilege to feed these fish to Karambwan!
2	line	Player	Just try it.
2	box	Tiadeche hesitates, then loads the Karambwanji in his net.
2	line	Tiadeche	This attracts many more Karambwan, but they still break free of the net.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player gives Tiadeche a Karambwan vessel with a raw Karambwanji inside:
2	line	Player	Tiadeche, instead of using your net, try using this vessel.
2	box	You hand over the Karambwan vessel to Tiadeche.
2	line	Tiadeche	What is it?
2	line	Player	It has been specially constructed to catch Karambwan. Once they enter it, they cannot return..
2	line	Player	Also, it has been loaded with Karambwanji. The Karambwan will not be able to resist this bait.
2	line	Tiadeche	As you say, Bwana.
2	line	Tiadeche	Bwana! I cannot believe my eyes!
2	line	Tiadeche	I, Tiadeche, who would never amount to anything, have managed to trap a Karambwan!
2	line	Tiadeche	Let me offer to you my first catch as a sign of gratitude.
2	select	Accept Tiadeche's offer?
2	option	Yes
3	box	Tiadeche hands you his first catch!
3	action	
3	line	Player	Your father would be proud.
3	line	Tiadeche	Hmph ... my father would not care.
3	line	Player	Speaking of your father, can we make way to the village? He awaits your return.
3	action	Continues below
2	option	No
3	line	Player	I have no need for it, Tiadeche.
3	line	Player	We must return to the village now.
3	action	Continues below
2	line	Tiadeche	I cannot return just yet. We witness the change of a turning tide. The secrets of the Karambwan are to be unlocked!
2	line	Player	...
2	line	Tiadeche	Before I return, I must ask you to do one thing.
2	line	Player	And that is?
2	line	Tiadeche	Take a Karambwan vessel to my brother Tinsay. He is the academic amongst us. Tell him I have asked him to study it so that we may craft more of its type.
2	line	Player	Can I have the vessel back then?
2	line	Tiadeche	I need this to practice with. Why don't you craft another one?
2	line	Player	I ... never mind.
2	action	end
0	section	Subsequent dialogue with Tiadeche
1	cond	If the player has not received (another?) Karambwan
2	line	Tiadeche	I have caught another Karambwan! I think I ought to give it to you.
2	action	
1	line	Tiadeche	Have you taken the Karambwan vessel to Tinsay?
1	cond	If the player has done so:
2	line	Player	Yes, I have.
2	line	Tiadeche	Did you ask for crafting instructions as I said?
2	cond	If the player does not have the crafting manual:
3	line	Player	I did, but I think I've lost them...
3	line	Tiadeche	Well go back and ask him to make another copy!
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has the crafting manual:
3	line	Player	Yes. He gave me this.
3	box	You hand over the crafting manual to Tiadeche.
3	line	Tiadeche	Thank you so much. You cannot understand what all of this means to me and our people.
3	line	Player	Will you return to the village now?
3	line	Tiadeche	Yes. I will do as I promised.
3	line	Player	I am glad to hear this. Let us go.
3	line	Tiadeche	Not yet. I will stay here a while to catch more Karambwan.
3	line	Tiadeche	I will meet you in the village once you have helped my brothers and spoken to my father.
3	action	end
1	cond	If the player has not done so:
2	line	Player	No, not yet.
2	line	Tiadeche	Please hurry! Time is of the essence!
2	action	end
0	section	Fishing at the Karambwan fishing spot without a Karambwan vessel
1	box	You need a Karambwan vessel to fish here.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Tamayu
1	line	Player	Tamayu, first son of Timfraku!
1	line	Tamayu	What do you want, stranger?
1	line	Player	Tamayu, I bring good news. Trufitus has communed with the gods - your village is once again safe.
1	line	Player	Your father requests that you return to the village.
1	line	Tamayu	Then know this, stranger.
1	line	Tamayu	I vow upon the blood of my fallen kin that I shall not set foot in that godforsaken village till I have slain the Shaikahan.
1	line	Player	You could slay it after we return to the village.
1	line	Tamayu	No! Your pitiful whining tires me. Now let me prepare.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Tamayu again
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Tell me more of the Shaikahan.
2	option	Dialogue 1
3	line	Player	Tell me more of the Shaikahan.
3	line	Tamayu	A source of indescribable evil. A beast more foul than your dreams could imagine. It hunts the jungle for anything foolish enough to cross its path.
3	action	initial
1	option	How long have you been hunting the Shaikahan?
2	line	Player	How long have you been hunting the Shaikahan?
2	line	Tamayu	Since before I was born, stranger. It is my destiny.
1	option	When will you succeed?
2	line	Player	When will you succeed?
2	line	Tamayu	When the gods bless me with success. You may join me on my next hunt, but you may not take part.
2	select	Follow Tamayu on the next hunt?
2	option	Yes
3	line	Player	Lead the way.
3	action	Tamayu attempts to defeat the Shaikahan with his bronze spear...
3	line	Tamayu	Shaikhan is at present far too agile for me!
3	line	Tamayu	I cannot do enough damage with this spear...
3	line	Tamayu	... and it seems to be healing too quickly!
3	action	end
2	option	No
3	line	Player	Perhaps later, Tamayu, first son of Timfraku.
3	action	end
1	option	I could slay the Shaikahan for you.
2	line	Player	I could slay the Shaikahan for you.
2	line	Tamayu	You offer to kill the beast for me? Stop this nonsense, lest I kill you first. It is I who must avenge the death of my kin.
2	action	end
1	option	I have already slain the Shaikahan!
2	line	Player	I have already slain the Shaikahan!
2	line	Tamayu	That is but an illusion. I still feel his evil in the wind. I must kill the Shaikahan myself.
2	action	end
