1	line	Lubufu	So I see. What would a fool like you want with me?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Talk about him...
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Who are you?
3	line	Player	Who are you?
3	line	Lubufu	I am Lubufu, son of Kedoaba, brother of Kedenda and second cousin twice removed of Ibeli!
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Who is Kedoaba?
4	line	Player	Who is Kedoaba?
4	line	Lubufu	Kedoaba is my father, the father of Kedenda and second uncle twice removed of Ibeli!
4	action	initial
3	option	Who is Kedenda?
4	line	Player	Who is Kedenda?
4	line	Lubufu	Kedenda is the son of my father, my brother and second cousin twice removed of Ibeli!
4	action	initial
3	option	Who is Ibeli?
4	line	Player	Who is Ibeli?
4	line	Lubufu	Ibeli is the second nephew twice removed of my father, and the second cousin twice removed of myself and my brother!
4	action	initial
3	option	Do you have any children?
4	line	Player	Do you have any children?
4	line	Lubufu	Alas, no. Focussed and determined in my trade as I was, I never found a suitable wife.
4	line	Lubufu	It is a great shame that the secret of the Karambwan has to die with me.
4	line	Player	You could tell me the secret...
4	line	Lubufu	Hah! What a stupid thought! The secret is mine and mine alone!
4	action	initial
2	option	Where are you from?
3	line	Player	Where are you from?
3	line	Lubufu	Our island of Karamja. Long ago, before you were even a thought in the back of a mind, I used to play on these beaches with the pebbles and stones.
3	line	Player	So you didn't have many friends then?
3	line	Lubufu	Silence!
3	line	Lubufu	As I grew older the ways of the world became apparent to me, and my attention turned from the rocks of the land to the fish in the sea.
3	line	Player	And ... ?
3	line	Lubufu	Despite what you might hear, there are plenty of fish in the sea! Especially when they can only be caught by me!
3	action	initial
2	option	What do you do?
3	line	Player	What do you do?
3	line	Lubufu	Nowadays I mostly fish for Karambwan and collect their bait. Collecting the bait has become increasingly tiresome, what with my age and health.
3	action	initial
2	option	How old are you?
3	line	Player	How old are you?
3	line	Lubufu	An order of magnitude older than you! What an impudent question! Collecting bait has become hard enough at this age as it is without having to endure the chiding of you young people!
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Which other young people come by here?
4	line	Player	Which other young people come by here?
4	cond	Unknown condition:
5	line	Lubufu	Hmm ... nobody I can recall right now.
5	action	previous
4	cond	Unknown condition:
5	line	Lubufu	I remember talking to a [lad/lass] by the name of [other player name] a while ago...
5	action	previous
3	option	What do you use for bait?
4	line	Player	What do you use for bait?
4	line	Lubufu	That is part of the secret! Why would I tell you?
4	action	previous
3	option	I could help collect the bait.
4	line	Player	I could help collect the bait.
4	line	Lubufu	And why would you help me?
4	select	Select an option
4	option	You sound like you could do with the help.
5	line	Player	You sound like you could do with the help.
5	line	Lubufu	Well perhaps you're right. It's nigh time I could do with some help after all.
5	line	Lubufu	I have a fair amount of bait left over since last time I collected some, but I will be needing more shortly.
5	line	Player	Ok. Where can I find the bait? I don't even know what it is!
5	line	Lubufu	Patience. I have kept the nature of the Karambwan a closely guarded secret. There is nobody alive who knows more about them than I do. Furthermore, there is nobody alive who even knows how they feed.
5	line	Lubufu	You must therefore understand that what I am about to tell you is given in complete trust, and that you are to tell nobody else.
5	line	Player	I understand.
5	line	Lubufu	Very well. The Karambwan are a form of octopus native to our island of Karamja. They feed solely on Karambwanji, a brightly coloured fish which also inhabits the coastal waters surrounding the island.
5	line	Lubufu	Karambwanji congregate in coastal shoals near the Holy Lake. You will find it easiest to fish for them there.
5	line	Player	Where is the Holy Lake?
5	line	Lubufu	Just to the south of Tai Bwo Wannai Village. I'm sure you've met the locals already.
5	line	Player	And what do I use to fish for the bait?
5	line	Lubufu	Any small net will do. Return here as soon as you have caught 20 Karambwanji.
5	action	end
4	option	You sound like you need help.
5	line	Player	You sound like you need help.
5	line	Lubufu	How dare you say such a thing! Be off with you!
5	action	end
4	option	I enjoy collecting meaningless items for people.
5	line	Player	I enjoy collecting meaningless items for people.
5	line	Lubufu	Meaningless? You know nothing of the Karambwan! Now leave!
5	action	end
4	option	You're right. I don't want to help.
5	line	Player	You're right. I don't want to help.
5	line	Lubufu	I didn't for one moment think you did.
5	action	initial
2	option	Talk about Karambwan...
3	select	Select an option
3	option	What is a Karambwan?
4	line	Player	What is a Karambwan?
4	line	Lubufu	A species of octopus native to the island which I and I alone know how to catch.
4	action	initial
3	option	What do you do with your Karambwan?
4	line	Player	What do you do with your Karambwan?
4	line	Lubufu	I eat what I need and sell the rest to the Shrimp and Parrot restaurant.
4	line	Player	Where is the Shrimp and Parrot?
4	line	Lubufu	You don't know anything do you? Just north of here, in Brimhaven!
4	action	initial
3	option	What do you use for bait?
4	line	Player	What do you use for bait?
4	line	Lubufu	That is part of the secret! Why would I tell you?
4	action	initial
3	option	What does Karambwan taste like?
4	line	Player	What does Karambwan taste like?
4	line	Lubufu	That depends entirely on how it is cooked...
4	line	Player	What do you mean?
4	line	Lubufu	Novicely cooked Karambwan is often poisonous to large mammals such as humans. If you buy some and cook it, be careful.
4	action	initial
2	option	Talk about something else...
3	select	Select an option
3	option	I have come for your soul.
4	line	Player	I have come for your soul.
4	line	Lubufu	Well you've wasted your time. My soul is long gone, along with my compassion.
4	action	previous
3	option	I'm with the Fishing Guild Anti-Monopoly Department.
4	line	Player	I'm from the Fishing Guild Anti-Monopoly Department.
4	line	Lubufu	And I'm from the Island Karamja. What do you want?
4	line	Player	We demand that you hand over the secret of the Karambwan.
4	line	Lubufu	Erm ... no.
4	line	Player	Oh, ok then. It was worth a try.
4	action	previous
3	option	Do you have any spare monkey skin lying around?
4	line	Player	Do you have any spare monkey skin lying around?
4	line	Lubufu	Funny you should say that...
4	line	Player	Why's that? Do you have any?
4	line	Lubufu	Well, people have been asking me for monkey skins all day!
4	line	Lubufu	But no, I'm out of monkey skin.
4	action	previous
3	option	I've heard something about an accident.
4	line	Player	I've heard something about an accident.
4	line	Lubufu	You will want to ask one of the tribesmen. I don't usually talk about it.
4	action	previous
2	option	Leave
0	section	Delivering raw Karambwanji to Lubufu
1	line	Lubufu	Have you retrieved the Karambwanji yet?
2	line	Player	Yes, I have some here.
2	cond	If the player has all 20 raw Karambwanji:
3	box	You hand Lubufu 20 raw Karambwanji.
3	line	Lubufu	Thank you! This should tide me over for the next month.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has some raw Karambwanji:
3	box	You hand Lubufu [#] raw Karambwanji.
3	line	Lubufu	Hurry along now. I still need [#] more.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player does not have 20 Karambwanji:
3	line	Player	No, I'm still fishing for them.
3	line	Lubufu	Well hurry! My reserves are beginning to run low.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player has the rest of the Karambwanji:
3	line	Lubufu	Have you retrieved the Karambwanji yet?
3	line	Lubufu	I still need [#] more.
3	line	Player	Yes, I have some here.
3	box	You hand Lubufu [#] raw Karambwanji.
3	line	Lubufu	Thank you! This should tide me over for the next month.
3	action	end
0	section	Talking to Lubufu after delivering raw Karambwanji
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What is a Karambwan?
2	line	Player	What is a Karambwan?
2	line	Lubufu	A species of octopus native to the island which I and I alone know how to catch.
2	line	Lubufu	You should really ought to know that by now.
2	action	initial
1	option	What do you do with your Karambwan?
2	action	above
1	option	What do you use to catch Karambwan?
2	line	Player	What do you use to catch Karambwan?
2	line	Lubufu	Well ... since you ask, a specially constructed octopus pot. But don't tell anybody - that's part of the secret!
2	line	Lubufu	My, you're keen aren't you?
2	line	Lubufu	How would you feel about becoming my apprentice?
2	line	Player	That's a slight change in attitude...
2	line	Lubufu	As much as I need to protect the secret, I should not carry it to the grave.
2	line	Lubufu	You seem a trustworthy type of person. Do you want to train as my apprentice?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes!
3	line	Player	Yes!
3	line	Lubufu	I'm glad to hear it. I'm sure the secrets of the Karambwan will be safe with you.
3	box	Lubufu teaches you a new fishing technique.
3	line	Lubufu	In our language, Karambwan literally means 'Friend of Karamja.' As a friend of mine I will now show you how to fish for them.
3	line	Lubufu	There are two aspects to fishing for Karambwan. Firstly, you must have the correct bait. Secondly, you must have the correct equipment.
3	line	Lubufu	You already know of the Karambwanji, which shoal in the Holy Lake to the south. As I have explained, the Karambwan feed only on the Karambwanji, which are therefore the perfect bait.
3	line	Player	But what kind of equipment do you use?
3	line	Lubufu	It is futile to attempt to catch Karambwan with something as basic as a net. They are too strong and vicious to be caught in such a fashion.
3	line	Lubufu	I have spent many years designing a specially shaped vessel, into which Karambwan may pass but from which they may not return.
3	line	Lubufu	If this vessel is loaded with Karambwanji, and then repeatedly lowered into a Karambwan shoal, then you should shortly find a Karambwan octopus trapped inside.
3	line	Lubufu	I will now give you a Karambwan fishing vessel with which you can practise. Make sure you do not lose it. Under no circumstance may you give or show this to anybody. Do you understand?
3	line	Player	Yes, I understand.
3	box	Lubufu hands you a Karambwan vessel.
3	line	Lubufu	Feel free to practise on my fishing spot.
3	action	
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	No.
3	line	Lubufu	Well the offer remains open. You're the most trustworthy person I have met in a long time.
3	line	Lubufu	Let me know if you change your mind.
3	action	end
1	option	What does Karambwan taste like?
2	action	above
0	section	Subsequent dialogue with Lubufu
1	line	Lubufu	How fares my apprentice?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	I'm fine thanks.
2	line	Player	I'm fine thanks.
2	line	Lubufu	And I'm glad to hear it!
2	action	end
1	option	I've been catching a whole load of Karambwan!
2	line	Player	I've been catching a whole load of Karambwan!
2	line	Lubufu	Look at you - outgrowing your boots already!
2	action	end
1	option	Actually, I've lost my Karambwan vessel.
2	line	Player	Actually, I've lost my Karambwan vessel.
2	line	Lubufu	You did what!? I hope nobody else has seen it...
2	line	Player	Don't worry - nobody will find it...
2	select	Select an option
2	option	... a shark ate it!
3	line	Player	... a shark ate it!
3	line	Lubufu	Well you'd better hope for your sake that this shark is never caught!
3	action	continue
2	option	... a Karambwan stole it!
3	line	Player	... a Karambwan stole it!
3	line	Lubufu	Well you'd better hope for your sake that this Karambwan is never caught!
3	action	continue
2	option	... it floated away!
3	line	Player	... it floated away!
3	line	Lubufu	Well you'd better hope for your sake that it never floats back!
3	line	Lubufu	In the meantime, you can practise with this.
3	box	Lubufu hands you a Karambwan vessel.
3	action	
3	line	Player	Thank you so much.
3	line	Lubufu	Don't mention it. I mean that.
3	action	end
1	option	Awful!
2	line	Player	Awful!
2	line	Lubufu	Why?
2	line	Player	Everybody keeps asking me to run around and do their errands!
2	line	Lubufu	Living the hard life of a fisherman now, eh.
2	action	end
